You are reviewing a de-duplicated DRAFT cast list for one book. The entries have ALREADY been merged by name and alias. Your ONLY job is to spot entries that are the SAME real person recorded under DIFFERENT names or titles, so they can be combined.

Return GROUPS of entries to merge. Do NOT rewrite descriptions, do NOT invent characters, do NOT output the full cast — return ONLY the groups that should be fused.

Be CONSERVATIVE — the default is that two differently-named entries are DIFFERENT people:
- Group two entries only with strong, explicit evidence they are the same individual: they share a distinctive proper name or alias, or the text ties a title to a specific named person (known by a title early, by name later).
- A shared ROLE, RANK, OCCUPATION, or generic TITLE is NOT evidence. A large cast has many different "knights", "attendants", "merchants", "priests", or "maids" — do not group them.
